window.PROCESS_TASKS["01"] = {"number":"01","title":"Manufacturing Bricks","icon":"🧱","image":"bricks.png","type":"Linear","stages":7,"description":"Quy trình sản xuất gạch từ đất sét đến đóng gói và vận chuyển.","prompt":"The diagram shows the process by which bricks are manufactured for the building industry.","analysis":{"type":["linear"],"stages":["7","seven"],"first":["clay","dug","ground"],"last":["brick","deliver","delivery","package","packaged"],"features":["crush","screen","grid","sand","water","shape","mould","mold","wire cutter","dry","heat","kiln","cool"],"body1":["clay","dig","grid","roller","sand","water","shape","mould","mold","wire cutter","dry"],"body2":["kiln","moderate","high","cool","package","deliver"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of bricks.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["production","manufacturing","manufacture"],["bricks","brick"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, the procedure follows a linear, seven-stage sequence that begins with clay being dug from the ground and ends with finished bricks being delivered. During these stages, the clay is crushed and mixed with sand and water, shaped, dried, heated and cooled before the bricks are packaged and transported.","concepts":[["overall"],["linear"],["seven","7"],["clay"],["dug","excavated","extracted"],["delivered","transported"],["crushed","screened","mixed"],["shaped","moulded","molded","cut"],["dried"],["heated","fired"],["cooled"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"In the initial stages, clay is extracted from the ground by a digger and passed through a metal grid, after which it is broken down by a roller. Sand and water are then added to the clay, and the resulting mixture is shaped into bricks either with a mould or a wire cutter. These raw bricks are subsequently dried in an oven for 24–48 hours.","concepts":[["clay"],["dug","excavated","extracted"],["metal grid","grid"],["roller"],["sand"],["water"],["mould","mold","wire cutter","shaped","cut"],["dried","drying oven","oven"],["24","48"]],"minWords":50,"sequence":["then","after","after which","subsequently","once","before"]},"body2":{"reference":"The remaining stages involve heating, cooling and delivery. The dried bricks are fired first in a kiln at a moderate temperature of 200–980°C and then at a higher temperature of 870–1300°C. They are then cooled in a chamber for 48–72 hours before being packaged and delivered.","concepts":[["kiln"],["moderate","200","980"],["high","870","1300"],["cooled","cooling chamber"],["48","72"],["packaged","packed"],["delivered","transported"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["first","then","after","before","subsequently"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of bricks.\n\nOverall, the procedure follows a linear, seven-stage sequence that begins with clay being dug from the ground and ends with finished bricks being delivered. During these stages, the clay is crushed and mixed with sand and water, shaped, dried, heated and cooled before the bricks are packaged and transported.\n\nIn the initial stages, clay is extracted from the ground by a digger and passed through a metal grid, after which it is broken down by a roller. Sand and water are then added to the clay, and the resulting mixture is shaped into bricks either with a mould or a wire cutter. These raw bricks are subsequently dried in an oven for 24–48 hours.\n\nThe remaining stages involve heating, cooling and delivery. The dried bricks are fired first in a kiln at a moderate temperature of 200–980°C and then at a higher temperature of 870–1300°C. They are then cooled in a chamber for 48–72 hours before being packaged and delivered."};

window.PROCESS_TASKS["02"] = {"number":"02","title":"Manufacturing Instant Noodles","icon":"🍜","image":"instant-noodles.png","type":"Linear","stages":8,"description":"Quy trình sản xuất mì ăn liền từ bột mì đến cốc mì được dán nhãn và niêm phong.","prompt":"The diagram below shows how instant noodles are manufactured.","analysis":{"type":["linear"],"stages":["8","eight"],"first":["flour","storage silo","silos","mixer"],"last":["cup","label","seal","sealed","labelled","labeled"],"features":["flour","water","oil","roller","sheet","strip","disc","cook","dry","cup","vegetable","spice","seal","label"],"body1":["flour","silo","mixer","water","oil","roller","sheet","strip","disc"],"body2":["cook","oil","dry","cup","vegetable","spice","seal","label"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of instant noodles.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["production","manufacturing","manufacture"],["instant noodles","noodles"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, the procedure is a linear, eight-stage process that begins with flour being taken from storage silos and ends with prepared noodle cups being sealed and labelled. During the process, the flour is mixed, rolled, cut and shaped before the noodle discs are cooked, dried and packaged with vegetables and spices.","concepts":[["overall"],["linear"],["eight","8"],["flour"],["storage silos","silos"],["sealed","seal"],["labelled","labeled","label"],["mixed","mixer"],["rolled","rollers"],["cut","strips"],["discs"],["cooked"],["dried"],["vegetables","spices"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"In the initial stages, ingredients are combined and formed into noodle portions. Flour is taken from storage silos and transferred to a mixer, where water and oil are added. Once the ingredients have been blended, the mixture passes through a set of rotating rollers, which flatten it into sheets that are then cut into strips before being shaped into round discs.","concepts":[["flour"],["storage silos","silos"],["mixer"],["water"],["oil"],["rollers","roller"],["sheets","dough sheets"],["strips","dough strips"],["discs","noodle discs"]],"minWords":50,"sequence":["once","then","before","after","following"]},"body2":{"reference":"The remaining stages deal with heat treatment and final assembly. The noodle discs are cooked in oil and subsequently dried as they move along the production line. After this stage has been completed, the dried noodles are placed into individual cups, and vegetables and spices are added before the filled cups are sealed and labelled, completing the manufacturing process.","concepts":[["cooked","cooking"],["oil"],["dried","drying"],["cups"],["vegetables"],["spices"],["sealed","sealing"],["labelled","labeled","labelling","labeling"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["subsequently","after","before","then","following"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of instant noodles.\n\nOverall, the procedure is a linear, eight-stage process that begins with flour being taken from storage silos and ends with prepared noodle cups being sealed and labelled. During the process, the flour is mixed, rolled, cut and shaped before the noodle discs are cooked, dried and packaged with vegetables and spices.\n\nIn the initial stages, ingredients are combined and formed into noodle portions. Flour is taken from storage silos and transferred to a mixer, where water and oil are added. Once the ingredients have been blended, the mixture passes through a set of rotating rollers, which flatten it into sheets that are then cut into strips before being shaped into round discs.\n\nThe remaining stages deal with heat treatment and final assembly. The noodle discs are cooked in oil and subsequently dried as they move along the production line. After this stage has been completed, the dried noodles are placed into individual cups, and vegetables and spices are added before the filled cups are sealed and labelled, completing the manufacturing process."};

window.PROCESS_TASKS["03"] = {"number":"03","title":"Manufacturing Tomato Ketchup","icon":"🍅","image":"tomato-ketchup.png","type":"Linear","stages":15,"description":"Quy trình sản xuất tương cà chua từ thu hoạch đến đóng chai, kiểm tra và phân phối.","prompt":"The diagram shows the process used to produce tomato ketchup.","analysis":{"type":["linear"],"stages":["15","fifteen"],"first":["tomato","pick","picked","harvest"],"last":["ketchup","hamburger","fries","consume","consumed","serve","served"],"features":["sort","factory","stalk","seed","skin","crush","sugar","vinegar","salt","boil","two hours","bottle","label","quality","pack","supermarket"],"body1":["pick","sort","factory","remove","stalk","seed","skin","container","crush","sugar","vinegar","salt"],"body2":["boil","two hours","bottle","label","quality","pack","supermarket","hamburger","fries"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of tomato ketchup.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["production","manufacturing","produce"],["tomato ketchup","ketchup"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, ketchup production is a linear, fifteen-stage process that begins with tomatoes being picked and ends with the finished product being consumed. Broadly, the tomatoes are selected and prepared before the mixture is cooked, bottled, checked, packed and delivered to supermarkets.","concepts":[["overall"],["linear"],["fifteen","15"],["tomatoes"],["picked","harvested"],["consumed","served","hamburger","fries"],["selected","sorted"],["prepared","crushed"],["cooked","boiled"],["bottled"],["quality","checked"],["packed"],["delivered","supermarket"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"In the initial stages, ripe tomatoes are picked and placed in baskets before good tomatoes are separated from unsuitable ones. The selected fruit is transported to a factory, where the stalks, skins and seeds are removed. The tomatoes are then put into a container and crushed, after which sugar, vinegar and salt are added to the mixture.","concepts":[["picked","harvested"],["sorted","separated","good","bad"],["factory","transported","sent"],["stalk","stalks"],["skin","skins"],["seed","seeds"],["container"],["crushed"],["sugar"],["vinegar"],["salt"]],"minWords":50,"sequence":["before","then","after which","where","following"]},"body2":{"reference":"The remaining stages begin with the tomato mixture being boiled and then left for two hours. It is subsequently poured into bottles, which are labelled and checked for quality. The approved bottles are packed into boxes and transported to supermarkets, after which the ketchup is ready to be consumed with foods such as hamburgers and fries.","concepts":[["boiled","boiling"],["two hours","2 hours"],["bottles","bottled","poured"],["labelled","labeled"],["quality control","quality","checked"],["packed","boxes"],["supermarkets","delivered","transported"],["hamburger","fries","consumed"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["then","subsequently","after","after which","before"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in the production of tomato ketchup.\n\nOverall, ketchup production is a linear, fifteen-stage process that begins with tomatoes being picked and ends with the finished product being consumed. Broadly, the tomatoes are selected and prepared before the mixture is cooked, bottled, checked, packed and delivered to supermarkets.\n\nIn the initial stages, ripe tomatoes are picked and placed in baskets before good tomatoes are separated from unsuitable ones. The selected fruit is transported to a factory, where the stalks, skins and seeds are removed. The tomatoes are then put into a container and crushed, after which sugar, vinegar and salt are added to the mixture.\n\nThe remaining stages begin with the tomato mixture being boiled and then left for two hours. It is subsequently poured into bottles, which are labelled and checked for quality. The approved bottles are packed into boxes and transported to supermarkets, after which the ketchup is ready to be consumed with foods such as hamburgers and fries."};

window.PROCESS_TASKS["04"] = {"number":"04","title":"Frog Life Cycle","icon":"🐸","image":"frog-life-cycle-clean.webp?v=20261126-salmon6-frogclean1","type":"Life Cycle","stages":11,"description":"Vòng đời của ếch từ trứng, nòng nọc đến ếch trưởng thành.","prompt":"The diagram illustrates the different stages in the life cycle of a frog.","analysis":{"type":["life cycle","life-cycle","cycle"],"stages":["11","eleven"],"first":["egg","eggs"],"last":["adult frog","mature frog","adult"],"features":["embryo","tadpole","water plant","gill","tail","hind leg","front leg","young frog","adult frog"],"body1":["egg","embryo","tadpole","water plant","gill","tail"],"body2":["hind leg","food stored","front leg","tail shorter","young frog","adult frog"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the different stages in the life cycle of a frog.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["life cycle","life-cycle"],["frog"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, the frog life cycle consists of eleven main stages, beginning with eggs and progressing through several tadpole forms before a young frog develops into a mature adult. The main transformation is the gradual growth of legs and the loss of the tail as the animal changes from an aquatic tadpole into an adult frog.","concepts":[["overall"],["eleven","11"],["eggs"],["tadpole","tadpoles"],["young frog"],["adult frog","mature adult"],["legs","hind legs","front legs"],["tail"],["aquatic","water"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"In the initial stages of the cycle, eggs develop into embryos before hatching as tadpoles that cling to water plants. The young tadpoles initially breathe through external gills, while their tails continue to grow. As development continues, the body becomes larger and the hind legs begin to appear.","concepts":[["eggs"],["embryos","embryo"],["tadpoles","tadpole"],["water plants","water-plant","water plant"],["external gills","gills"],["tail"],["hind legs","hindlegs"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["before","initially","as","while","then"]},"body2":{"reference":"In the later stages, the developing frog relies on food stored in its tail while the front legs emerge. The tail then becomes progressively shorter and the animal turns into a young frog. Finally, it reaches the adult stage, after which mature frogs reproduce and the cycle begins again with new eggs.","concepts":[["food stored","stored in","tail"],["front legs","frontlegs"],["tail","shorter","shrinks"],["young frog"],["adult frog","adult stage"],["eggs","new eggs","reproduce"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["then","finally","after which","while","later"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the different stages in the life cycle of a frog.\n\nOverall, the frog life cycle consists of eleven main stages, beginning with eggs and progressing through several tadpole forms before a young frog develops into a mature adult. The main transformation is the gradual growth of legs and the loss of the tail as the animal changes from an aquatic tadpole into an adult frog.\n\nIn the initial stages of the cycle, eggs develop into embryos before hatching as tadpoles that cling to water plants. The young tadpoles initially breathe through external gills, while their tails continue to grow. As development continues, the body becomes larger and the hind legs begin to appear.\n\nIn the later stages, the developing frog relies on food stored in its tail while the front legs emerge. The tail then becomes progressively shorter and the animal turns into a young frog. Finally, it reaches the adult stage, after which mature frogs reproduce and the cycle begins again with new eggs."};

window.PROCESS_TASKS["05"] = {"number":"05","title":"Bee Life Cycle","icon":"🐝","image":"bee-life-cycle-premium.webp?v=20261126-premium4","type":"Life Cycle","stages":7,"description":"Vòng đời của ong từ khi con cái đẻ trứng đến khi con non trưởng thành.","prompt":"The diagram shows the life cycle of a bee, including the time taken for each developmental stage.","analysis":{"type":["life cycle","life-cycle","cycle"],"stages":["7","seven"],"first":["female","lay","egg","eggs"],"last":["maturity","mature","adult","female"],"features":["egg","hatch","9","10","moult","molting","young adult","maturity","34","36","third moult","third moulting","three moults"],"body1":["female","egg","9","10","first moulting","5 days"],"body2":["second moulting","7 days","young adult","9 days","4 days","maturity","third moult","third moulting","9 days"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the different stages in the life cycle of a bee.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["life cycle","life-cycle"],["bee","bees"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, this diagram presents seven visible stages and a 34–36-day life cycle. After hatching, the developing bee moults three times before a young adult emerges and eventually reaches maturity.","concepts":[["overall"],["seven","7"],["34","36"],["hatching","hatch"],["three moults","moults three times","third moult","third moulting"],["young adult"],["maturity","mature"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"The cycle begins when a female lays one or two eggs every three days. These hatch after around 9–10 days, after which the growing insect undergoes its first moult five days later and a second moult after a further seven days.","concepts":[["female"],["one or two","1 or 2"],["eggs"],["three days","3 days"],["hatch","hatched"],["9","10"],["first moult","first moulting"],["five days","5 days"],["second moult","second moulting"],["seven days","7 days"]],"minWords":40,"sequence":["beginning","after","later","then"]},"body2":{"reference":"A third moult occurs nine days after the second one. A young adult then emerges and takes another four days to become fully mature. The mature female can lay eggs to begin another cycle, which takes approximately 34–36 days in total.","concepts":[["third moult","third moulting","third molt"],["nine days","9 days"],["young adult"],["emerges","emerged"],["four days","4 days"],["mature","maturity"],["female","lay eggs"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["following","later","then","once","after"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the different stages in the life cycle of a bee.\n\nOverall, this diagram presents seven visible stages and a 34–36-day life cycle. After hatching, the developing bee moults three times before a young adult emerges and eventually reaches maturity.\n\nThe cycle begins when a female lays one or two eggs every three days. These hatch after around 9–10 days, after which the growing insect undergoes its first moult five days later and a second moult after a further seven days.\n\nA third moult occurs nine days after the second one. A young adult then emerges and takes another four days to become fully mature. The mature female can lay eggs to begin another cycle, which takes approximately 34–36 days in total."};

window.PROCESS_TASKS["06"] = {"number":"06","title":"Recycling Plastic Bottles","icon":"♻️","image":"plastic-bottles.png","type":"Cyclical","stages":9,"description":"Quy trình tái chế chai nhựa từ thu gom đến tạo ra nguyên liệu và sản phẩm mới.","prompt":"The diagram shows how plastic bottles are recycled.","analysis":{"type":["cyclical"],"stages":["9","nine"],"first":["plastic bottle","bottles","recycling bin","bin"],"last":["end products","new products","products","produced","manufactured"],"features":["bin","truck","sorting","compress","block","crush","wash","pellet","heat","raw material","end products"],"body1":["bin","truck","recycling centre","sorting","compress","block"],"body2":["crush","wash","pellet","heat","raw material","end products"]},"intro":{"reference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in recycling plastic bottles.","concepts":[["diagram","figure"],["illustrates","shows","depicts"],["recycling","recycled","recycle"],["plastic bottles","bottles"]],"minWords":8},"overview":{"reference":"Overall, this is a nine-stage recycling process with a potential repeat cycle that begins with used plastic bottles being placed in recycling bins and ends with recycled material being turned into new products. The bottles are collected and sorted before being compressed, crushed, washed and converted into pellets and raw material.","concepts":[["overall"],["linear"],["nine","9"],["plastic bottles","bottles"],["recycling bins","recycling bin"],["new products","end products"],["sorted"],["compressed"],["crushed"],["washed"],["pellets"],["raw material"]],"minWords":35},"body1":{"reference":"In the initial stages, used plastic bottles are placed in recycling bins and collected by a truck, which transports them to a recycling centre. There, recyclable bottles are sorted from unsuitable waste and the selected plastic is compressed into large blocks ready for further processing.","concepts":[["recycling bins","recycling bin"],["truck"],["recycling centre","recycling center"],["sorted","sorting"],["compressed","compressing"],["blocks","block"]],"minWords":40,"sequence":["there","then","after","which","before"]},"body2":{"reference":"The remaining stages involve converting the plastic into reusable material. The compressed blocks are crushed into small pieces and washed before being processed into plastic pellets. These pellets are then heated to form raw material, which is used to manufacture a range of end products, including new plastic containers.","concepts":[["crushed","crushing"],["washed","washing"],["plastic pellets","pellets"],["heated","heating"],["raw material"],["end products","new products","manufacture","produced"]],"minWords":45,"sequence":["before","then","which","after","remaining"]},"fullReference":"The diagram illustrates the stages involved in recycling plastic bottles.\n\nOverall, this is a nine-stage recycling process with a potential repeat cycle that begins with used plastic bottles being placed in recycling bins and ends with recycled material being turned into new products. The bottles are collected and sorted before being compressed, crushed, washed and converted into pellets and raw material.\n\nIn the initial stages, used plastic bottles are placed in recycling bins and collected by a truck, which transports them to a recycling centre. There, recyclable bottles are sorted from unsuitable waste and the selected plastic is compressed into large blocks ready for further processing.\n\nThe remaining stages involve converting the plastic into reusable material. The compressed blocks are crushed into small pieces and washed before being processed into plastic pellets. These pellets are then heated to form raw material, which is used to manufacture a range of end products, including new plastic containers.","category":"CyclicalProcess"};

